   image gate: murdoch_house_2130_prairie chicagology_2140_a: verdict "differs", 3 difference(s) open: the stack: the print's one visible stack stands on the ridge just left of the tower's cone (x 1598-1645 px, top about y 675), short and broad; the build's stacks stand at u 13.0 and u 3.0, far behind it, and none stands there (with the roof over the front, above, it moves with that roof); the roof over the front: the build carries the front up as a steep street gable to 15.4 m (shaped_gable), its apex standing in the sky beside the tower's cone; neither picture shows any gable on the street front. Both show instead the south flank rising into a gable of rock-faced stone over its front part (the Chicagology print: its apex at about (1487, 662) px, on this camera about 13.5 m over grade and 2.3 m behind the front, with one attic light in it at x 1460-1490, y 790-860) and a slated roof whose ridge runs along the avenue from that apex to the tower's cone (near level at y 690-700 across x 1490-1690), its east slope falling to the front's eave. A side-gabled front block behind the tower, which K01's shaped_gable and hip do not stand; one difference, both pictures; the columned porch across the front's south end (posts and an entablature at about the principal floor's head, the Chicagology print's x 1460-1680 px, y 1030-1200, the Van Osdel print's x 546-575, y 399-440): not built, the door stands bare at the top of the stoop (L-k01-2130-murdoch-3729: no K01 part stands a recessed porch under a front)
